      "part_type": "Hadith",
      "path": "/books/al-kafi:6:6:125:1",
      "text": [
        " أَكْلُ الْجَزَرِ يُسَخِّنُ الْكُلْيَتَيْنِ وَ يُقِيمُ الذَّكَرَ ."
      ],
      "translations": {
        "en.hubeali": [
          "Muhammad Bin Yahya, from Ahmad Bin Muhammad Bin Al Hassan Bin Ali, or someone else, from Dawood Bin Farqad, ",
          "(It has been narrated) from Abu Abdullah<sup>asws</sup> having said: ‘Eating the carrots warms the kidneys and stirs the manhood’."
        ],
        "en.sarwar": [
          "1. Muhammad ibn Yahya has narrated from Ahmad ibn Muhammad from al-Hassan ibn Ali and others from Dawud ibn Farqad who has said the following: “Abu ’Abd Allah, ‘Alayhi al-Salam, has said, ’Eating carrot warms up the kidneys and causes erection.”’ "
        ]
      }
